SYSTEM-WIDE IT NOTICE
Tarrow IT Services | System-wide IT all-staff notices
Audience: all staff and faculty, System Office and all campuses

Multi-factor sign-in becomes mandatory on Monday 15 March 2027

Dear colleagues,

Starting Monday 15 March 2027, multi-factor authentication (MFA) will be
required every time you sign in to your Tarrow account from outside the
campus network, and once every 14 days on campus. This applies to email,
calendar, chat, the HR and payroll portal, and every application that
uses the Tarrow single sign-on page.

What you need to do before 15 March

  - Enroll at least one second factor. The Tarrow Authenticator app is
    recommended; a hardware key or a text message to a mobile phone
    also works.
  - Enroll a backup method as well, so a lost or replaced phone does not
    lock you out.
  - Check that the mobile number on your account is current.
  - If you already use MFA for the payroll portal, you are enrolled and
    need to do nothing further.

Step-by-step enrollment guide (5 minutes):
https://itservices.tarrow.example/kb/mfa-enrollment

What changes on 15 March

  - Accounts without a registered second factor will be prompted to
    enroll at next sign-in and cannot continue until they do.
  - Shared and departmental mailboxes are not affected; individual
    accounts with delegated access to them are.
  - Service accounts and room devices are handled separately by your
    campus IT team. No action is needed from individual staff.

Help

  - Tarrow IT Services Desk: Monday to Friday, 07:00-19:00;
    Saturday, 09:00-13:00.
  - Phone: extension 4-HELP (4-4357) from any campus phone.
  - Drop-in enrollment help: System Office lobby, Tuesdays and
    Thursdays 12:00-14:00 until 12 March.
  - Campus service desks can also help with enrollment.

A reminder about phishing

  - Tarrow IT Services will NEVER ask for your password, by email,
    phone, chat or text.
  - We will never ask you to approve a sign-in prompt you did not start.
    If you receive one, deny it and call the IT Services Desk.
  - Expect a rise in fake "MFA enrollment" emails over the next few
    weeks. The only genuine enrollment page is the one linked above.
    When in doubt, type the address yourself rather than clicking.

Thank you for helping keep Tarrow accounts and student data secure.

